From 83006037e17c573fede0d0b4d78e7617dfc52988 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "exe.dev user" <exedev@erbium-qemu.exe.xyz>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:13:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] sw-sysemu(erbium): SocketAgent host API (--api-socket)
 and --mram-file

Implements the QEMU <-> erbium_emu control protocol v1 (docs/protocol.md)
as an api_communicate on a listening UNIX socket:

* --api-socket PATH: SocketAgent accepts one client at a time, services
  all complete requests per main-loop iteration with non-blocking reads
  and a reassembly buffer (partial and pipelined messages handled).
  READ/WRITE go through MainMemory with a Noagent, split at region
  boundaries and into 4/8-byte units in register regions; memory_error
  -> DECERR, misaligned register access / other exceptions -> SLVERR,
  bad header/len -> BADREQ (corrupt header also drops the connection).
  PING returns erb_info{1, 0, 0x40000000, 16MiB, "erbium_emu"}.
  RESET kind 0 -> sys_emu::por_reset() (sysregs/SCCR + cold/warm reset of
  the harts, memory preserved), kind 1 -> no-op.
* --mram-file PATH: back MRAM with the shared file (MmapRegion).
* api_communicate::keep_alive()/idle_wait(): with the socket the main loop
  keeps running with no active harts and blocks in poll() for 1 ms per
  iteration when idle (no timers running) instead of spinning.
  --api-socket also lifts the default -max_cycles limit and the
  'need an ELF' check.
* FATAL chip errors while serving a host take the harts offline
  (sys_emu::stop_all_harts) instead of ending the emulation; a host POR
  brings them back.
* SIGINT/SIGTERM end the emulation cleanly (socket file unlinked).

Co-authored-by: Shelley <shelley@exe.dev>
